From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Mon, 7 Feb 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: fold the players that Lua sees at n > 2 (scope, player
 param kind, fold.h)

While Lua runs for duelist P at n > 2, Lua now sees only 0 and 1.
0 is P (in Tag, the own team). 1 is the opponents.
Before, seats 2 and 3 got 1-tp = -1 or -2 and many scripts ended with Lua errors.

Scope: interpreter keeps a stack of Lua scopes (the duelist, the bound opponent,
yieldable, probe, touched). Every Lua entry pushes and pops one.
Each coroutine resume pushes it again. The trap build checks the depth after every entry.

Player param kind: LuaParam gets PLAYER. 135 add_param sites that push a seat
are changed from INT to PLAYER. 132 INT sites stay. 131 are not players.
1 is a seat that stays INT because the Domain anchor in operations.cpp (PayLPCost) holds the line.
PLAYER folds the value in a scope. Without a scope it is the old value.

fold.h: new helpers for the library (unfold_action, query_list, field_list,
field_side, for_each_other, for_each_target, matches, push_player).
The trap build writes NFOLD lines for kinds a, b and d to stderr. It never aborts.

Slice with the helpers: Duel.GetTurnPlayer, IsTurnPlayer, GetLP, Damage,
GetLocationCount, GetDecktopGroup, Card.GetControler, Card.IsControler.
The other library functions are for the next steps.

With 2 duelists nothing changes. No scope folds and every helper is the identity.
The n=2 message hashes stay the same.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
